{"request": {"upstream": "cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "fork_owner": "LucaKro", "branch": "world-copies-keep-simulator-properties"}, "recording": {"recorder": {"version": "0.0.1.dev399+g53488928a", "commit": "53488928a119f21d21bcbf3ab2aeceb9d2bc5c59"}, "answers": [{"transport": "rest pages", "address": "repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pulls?head=LucaKro:world-copies-keep-simulator-properties&state=all&per_page=100", "variables": {}, "answer": [[{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pulls/968", "id": 5298024471, "html_url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/968", "number": 968, "state": "open", "title": "Keep simulator properties and actuated degrees of freedom when copying and merging", "user": {"login": "LucaKro", "id": 90992250, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/LucaKro", "html_url": "https://github.com/LucaKro", "type": "User"}, "body": "Proposed from https://github.com/LucaKro/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/106", "created_at": "2026-11-13T15:17:05Z", "merged_at": null, "requested_reviewers": [{"login": "tomsch420", "id": 60885903, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/tomsch420", "html_url": "https://github.com/tomsch420", "type": "User"}], "labels": [{"id": 9818517350, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/labels/semDT", "name": "semDT", "color": "0e8a16", "description": ""}], "draft": false, "head": {"label": "LucaKro:world-copies-keep-simulator-properties", "ref": "world-copies-keep-simulator-properties", "sha": "61ac56309b9a739e821d7b03d86325d21f13df33", "user": {"login": "LucaKro", "id": 90992250, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/LucaKro", "html_url": "https://github.com/LucaKro", "type": "User"}, "repo": {"id": 1108016504, "name": "cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "full_name": "LucaKro/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "html_url": "https://github.com/LucaKro/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "description": null, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/LucaKro/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "created_at": "2025-12-01T23:04:54Z", "has_issues": true, "has_discussions": true, "default_branch": "main"}}, "base": {"label": "cram2:main", "ref": "main", "sha": "7b1f3456961f5b4074c190ca1e3832326096498a", "user": {"login": "cram2", "id": 11426926, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/cram2", "html_url": "https://github.com/cram2", "type": "Organization"}, "repo": {"id": 1107735865, "name": "cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "full_name": "cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "html_url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "description": "A cognitive architecture for the entire stack of robotics", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "created_at": "2025-12-01T14:44:16Z", "has_issues": true, "has_discussions": false, "default_branch": "main"}}}]]}, {"transport": "graphql", "address": "query ReviewThreadsPage(\n  $owner: String!\n  $name: String!\n  $number: Int!\n  $threadCursor: String\n) {\n  repository(owner: $owner, name: $name) {\n    pullRequest(number: $number) {\n      reviewThreads(first: 100, after: $threadCursor) {\n        pageInfo {\n          hasNextPage\n          endCursor\n        }\n        nodes {\n          id\n          isResolved\n          isOutdated\n          path\n          line\n          comments(first: 100) {\n            nodes {\n              databaseId\n              author {\n                login\n              }\n              body\n              createdAt\n              url\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "variables": {"owner": "cram2", "name": "cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "number": 968, "threadCursor": null}, "answer": {"repository": {"pullRequest": {"reviewThreads": {"pageInfo": {"hasNextPage": false, "endCursor": "Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpK0MjAyNi0xMS0xNlQxMTozNTo0OFrOt-cAhw=="}, "nodes": [{"id": "PRRT_kwDOQga1Oc635wB_", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": false, "path": "semantic_digital_twin/src/semantic_digital_twin/world_description/world_entity.py", "line": 288, "comments": {"nodes": [{"databaseId": 4585210014, "author": {"login": "ichumuh"}, "body": "This lookup is the slowdown. `get_world_entity_with_id_by_id` goes through `find_world_entity_with_id`, which scans every entity in the world, and it now runs for every parent, child and degree of freedom of every copied connection. That makes a world copy grow with the square of the entity count. The removed code used `get_kinematic_structure_entity_by_id` and `get_degree_of_freedom_by_id`, which are hash lookups.\n\nSuggested fix: have `find_world_entity_with_id` try `self._get_world_entity_by_hash(hash(entity_id))` first, and scan only for semantic annotations (the case its docstring describes). Alternatively, `_resolve_item` could call the typed getters directly.\n", "createdAt": "2026-11-16T11:35:48Z", "url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/968#discussion_r4585210014"}, {"databaseId": 4586257215, "author": {"login": "LucaKro"}, "body": "i see, sure makes sense", "createdAt": "2026-11-16T13:23:07Z", "url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/968#discussion_r4586257215"}]}}, {"id": "PRRT_kwDOQga1Oc635wCH", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": false, "path": "test/semantic_digital_twin_test/test_worlds/test_copies_keep_simulator_properties.py", "line": 163, "comments": {"nodes": [{"databaseId": 4585210025, "author": {"login": "ichumuh"}, "body": "Nit: this checks only the merged world's bodies. Please also assert that the receiving world's `simulator_additional_properties` are unchanged, since \"neither world is changed\" is the promise in the `merge_world` docstring.\n", "createdAt": "2026-11-16T11:35:48Z", "url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/968#discussion_r4585210025"}, {"databaseId": 4586252618, "author": {"login": "LucaKro"}, "body": "i agree", "createdAt": "2026-11-16T13:22:42Z", "url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/968#discussion_r4586252618"}]}}]}}}}}, {"transport": "rest pages", "address": "repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pulls/968/reviews?per_page=100", "variables": {}, "answer": [[{"id": 5919316980, "user": {"login": "ichumuh", "id": 4130471, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/ichumuh", "html_url": "https://github.com/ichumuh", "type": "User"}, "body": "Good direction: replacing the hand-written `copy_for_world` methods with the generic one fixes real bugs on main (properties dropped by several copies, `Connection6DoF`/`OmniDrive`/`DifferentialDrive` hard-coding their class, and every actuator losing its degrees of freedom in `deepcopy`). Checking unique properties before a merge changes anything is a sensible rule. I ran `test_worlds` and `test_connections` locally at 61ac56309b: 438 passed, 2 skipped.\n\nTwo things before merging:\n\n1. **`deepcopy` gets ~40% slower and grows with the square of world size.** PR2 + apartment, 5 runs each: 0.39 s on main, 0.56 s at 61ac56309b. The profile puts it on `World.get_world_entity_with_id_by_id`, not on the field introspection (about 0.02 s per copy). See the inline comment.\n2. **This PR's description is empty upstream.** It only links the fork PR, so reviewers here can't see what changes. When you copy the fork description over, change `Fixes #65` / `Fixes #68`: on this repository those numbers would close unrelated issues.\n\nNot blocking, but worth a look:\n\n- **The generic copy now skips state silently.** A private or `init=False` field is no longer copied, and nothing says so. That is exactly what lost `Actuator._dofs`. A test that sends one instance of every concrete `WorldEntityWithID` subclass through `deepcopy` and compares them would catch the next one.\n- **Actuators now keep degrees of freedom alive.** That is right for tendons. But removing a connection whose degree of freedom an actuator drives no longer deletes that degree of freedom; it stays until the actuator is removed. Is removing a robot guaranteed to remove its actuators? Validation is also stricter now: an actuator pointing at a degree of freedom the world doesn't hold raises.\n- **World-level properties aren't synchronized.** `merge_world` moves them with a plain append, not as a world modification, so the ROS world synchronizer won't carry them. `add_simulator_property` already behaves this way on main, but merge now relies on it.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n", "state": "COMMENTED", "html_url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/968#pullrequestreview-5919316980", "submitted_at": "2026-11-16T11:35:48Z"}, {"id": 5920664204, "user": {"login": "LucaKro", "id": 90992250, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/LucaKro", "html_url": "https://github.com/LucaKro", "type": "User"}, "body": "", "state": "COMMENTED", "html_url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/968#pullrequestreview-5920664204", "submitted_at": "2026-11-16T13:22:42Z"}, {"id": 5920671295, "user": {"login": "LucaKro", "id": 90992250, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/LucaKro", "html_url": "https://github.com/LucaKro", "type": "User"}, "body": "", "state": "COMMENTED", "html_url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/968#pullrequestreview-5920671295", "submitted_at": "2026-11-16T13:23:07Z"}]]}, {"transport": "rest", "address": "repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pulls/968", "variables": {}, "answer": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pulls/968", "id": 5298024471, "html_url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/968", "number": 968, "state": "open", "title": "Keep simulator properties and actuated degrees of freedom when copying and merging", "user": {"login": "LucaKro", "id": 90992250, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/LucaKro", "html_ur